# 📰 Fake News Detection using Machine Learning

## Overview

This project detects whether a news article is **Fake** or **Real** using Natural Language Processing (NLP) and Machine Learning.

The application is built with Streamlit and uses a trained Passive Aggressive Classifier along with a TF-IDF Vectorizer.


---
## Dataset

The datasets are not included in this repository because of their size.

Download:

- Fake.csv
- True.csv

Place them inside:

dataset/
## Features

- Detect Fake News
- Detect Real News
- NLP Text Cleaning
- TF-IDF Vectorization
- Streamlit Web App
- Interactive User Interface

---

## Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Scikit-learn
- NLTK
- Streamlit
- Joblib

---

## Machine Learning Workflow

1. Load Dataset
2. Clean Text
3. Remove Stopwords
4. Apply Stemming
5. TF-IDF Vectorization
6. Train Machine Learning Model
7. Evaluate Model
8. Save Model
9. Deploy with Streamlit

---

## Models Used

- Logistic Regression
- Multinomial Naive Bayes
- Passive Aggressive Classifier

---

## Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/hasnain670-web/-Fake-News-Detection.git

cd Fake-News-Detection

pip install -r requirements.txt

streamlit run app.py
```

